{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795259072,"nonce":"gt8qAI/f6RA53JtC+H7l24ODjlM=","message":"Components, agreed 2026-11-21: a @:component typedef is a schema only. The macro generates the array-backed storage and typed accessors, and the frame loop never allocates or reads per-entity anonymous objects (anonymous-structure field reads are lookups, not fixed offsets, on hxcpp and to a lesser extent HashLink). @:component also accepts a class (e.g. @:structInit) for types that need methods, with the same generated storage. Metadata on typedefs and their fields is supported (checked on Haxe 4.3.6), but it belongs to the typedef's name: macros must see the declared typedef type, since a structurally equal anonymous value carries no metadata.","files":null}]}